    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The US Navy&#39;s deployed carrier strike groups and amphibious ready groups have been tracked as of September 8, 2026. North Korea has commissioned the second Choe Hyon-class destroyer, Kang Kon, under the leadership of Kim Jong Un. The U.S. Navy has trialed a robotic towed connector to refuel an unmanned surface vessel, and the U.S. Navy has interdicted a second suspected narco logistics vessel in the Eastern Pacific. A Type 055-class guided-missile destroyer, Zunyi, has returned to service after a fatal collision incident with a China Coast Guard cutter. The U.S. Department of War News Feed highlights the 40th anniversary of the Goldwater–Nichols Defense Reform Act, which is considered one of the most important reforms in the U.S. military history. The U.S. Department of Military and Veterans Affairs recognized unique and innovative suicide prevention programs during a ceremony in the Pentagon&#39;s Hall of Heroes.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
